    "result_text": "The full suite passes: **64 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS.**\n\n## Summary\n\nI redesigned the owner identity key and duplicate-detection logic to match the spec.\n\n**`Owner.java`** (`src/main/java/.../model/Owner.java`)\n- `getIdentityKey()` now returns the lower-case hex **SHA-256** digest of `normalizedTelephone + '|' + lowerEmail + '|' + soundex(lastName)` (a 64-hex string), replacing the old plaintext `telephone|email|householdId` key.\n- Added a standard **American Soundex** implementation (`soundex`/`soundexDigit`) and a `sha256Hex` helper.\n\n**`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** (`addOwner`)\n- The 409 duplicate check still runs on `identityKey`, still ignoring soft-deleted owners, with the email-domain blocklist applied first \u2014 unchanged in structure but now keyed on the new SHA-256 identity.\n- **Removed** the separate household-duplicate 409 block (the one derived from the computed `householdId`). Two owners with the same last name and postcode but different telephones now have different identity keys, so both are created.\n- **Replaced** the hardcoded `possibleDuplicate = false` with the new **soft-match**: when the new owner's identity key differs from all existing (non-deleted) owners but its `soundex(lastName)` **and** postcode match one, it's flagged `possibleDuplicate = true` / `possibleDuplicateOf = <earliest matching owner id>`.\n- Kept `householdId`, `householdSize`, and the membership-level cap logic intact (still needed by other checkpoints).\n\n**`openapi.yml`** \u2014 updated the `identityKey` field description/example to reflect the SHA-256 formula.\n\nKey behaviour-change checkpoints (Cp10, Cp35 soft-match; Cp28, Cp52 SHA-256 shape + collision; Cp03/Cp25 identity 409) all pass, along with the household/membership tests (Cp11, Cp23, Cp39, Cp51) that depend on the retained household logic.",
